# Line endings are part of this repository's determinism contract.
#
# Nise's golden suites compare generated bytes against committed testdata
# byte for byte, and the generator normalizes CRLF out of template files
# (internal/generator/plan.go) precisely so a Windows checkout cannot change
# what a generated project contains. Testdata, however, is read raw. Without
# this file, a checkout on a machine with `core.autocrlf=true` — the Git for
# Windows default, and the default on GitHub's Windows runners — rewrites
# every text file to CRLF on the way to the working tree. Generation then
# emits LF while the committed golden on disk holds CRLF, and every golden
# comparison fails for a reason that has nothing to do with the code.
#
# Forcing LF in the working tree on every platform removes that whole class
# of failure. Go, gofmt, and the Node toolchain all read LF on Windows
# without complaint, so nothing here loses anything by it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be examined for line endings at all.
*.png binary
